# {{.Name}}

A Sora extension (panel template). The only bridge between this panel and
the app is `window.soraExt` - typed in `sora-ext.d.ts` next to this file.

## Develop

```sh
sora-ext dev        # serve with live reload on http://127.0.0.1:8377
sora-ext serve      # serve with a mocked window.soraExt (test in a desktop browser)
```

## Ship

```sh
sora-ext validate
sora-ext pack . -o {{.ID}}.soraext
sora-ext sign --key .sora/author.key {{.ID}}.soraext
sora-ext publish {{.ID}}.soraext
```

Docs: `docs/extensions-quickstart.md` (10-minute guide), `docs/extensions-api.md`
(API reference), `docs/extensions-cookbook.md` (recipes). Normative spec:
`docs/extensions.md`.

## Files

- `sora-extension.json` - manifest v1 (id `{{.ID}}`)
- `panel.html` - the panel
- `sora-ext.d.ts` - TypeScript definitions for `window.soraExt`
- `author.key` / `author.pub` - your signing keypair. **Keep `author.key`
  offline and never commit it.** If it leaks, generate a new one and
  re-sign; the public key in the manifest is what the app trusts.
